{
    "background_story": "Snookums was a gentle feline with a passion for flowers. Her owner, a kind old florist, would often take her on strolls through the garden. Among the blooms, one flower caught Snookums' eye: the delicate, fragrant dianthus. She'd spend hours sniffing and purring around the dianthus patch, as if mesmerized by their beauty. As the seasons changed, Snookums would watch over the dianthus, ensuring they received just the right amount of sun and water. When the flowers bloomed, she'd curl up beside them, basking in their sweet fragrance. The florist would smile, saying Snookums was the dianthus' loyal guardian angel. As the flowers wilted, Snookums would stay by their side, a symbol of devotion and love for the fleeting beauty of the dianthus.",
